-- title:
--   Local n-th powers on the crossing model are u U^jhⁿ
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring: a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal. Let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, let $m, n$ be positive natural numbers such that the image of $mn$ in $W$ is a unit and some $\zeta \in W$ is a primitive $mn$-th root of unity. Write $R_0 =$ `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ (m * n))` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{mn}$, and let $K_0$ be a field equipped with an $R_0$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R_0$. Let $f \in K_0$ be nonzero, and assume that for every prime ideal $P$ of $R_0$ of height $1$ there are $g \in K_0$ and $r, s \in R_0$, both outside $P$, with $f \cdot s = g^n \cdot r$ in $K_0$ (elements of $R_0$ being mapped into $K_0$ by the structure map). Then there are a unit $u$ of $R_0$, a natural number $j$ and $h \in K_0$ such that $f = u \cdot U(\pi^{mn})^j \cdot h^n$ in $K_0$, where $U(\pi^{mn})$ denotes the distinguished element `U (π ^ (m * n))` of $R_0$.
--
--   This is the divisor-class input to a Kummer-type classification on the crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{mn})$ of an $A_{mn-1}$ singularity: being an $n$-th power up to units locally at every height-one prime forces $f$ to be a unit times a power of the coordinate $U$ times a global $n$-th power, so the obstruction is carried by the single component $U$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_pow_eq_unit_mul_U_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_pow_eq_unit_mul_U_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul), and the hypotheses that $mn$ be invertible and that $W$ contain a primitive $mn$-th root of unity are what allow the passage to the regular model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_eq_unit_mul_U_pow_mul_pow_of_forall_height_eq_one_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul.lean

